{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>You have troubled me.</b> For shedding blood in vain; and he used the language of עכירה — just as one troubles wine with its dregs, so 'you have troubled me' among the inhabitants of the land, to bring upon me an evil name, that they may say, 'they did evil to men of peace with them.'" "<b>And in the Midrash,</b> <b>עכרתם אותי — you have troubled me:</b> the cask was clear and you troubled it. It was handed over to the Canaanites that they should fall by the hand of my sons, but they would say, 'until you multiply and inherit the land'; therefore they kept silent. <b>And I am men of number.</b> Few men."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:34.821720030Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}